@startuml 05_User_Joins_Conversation

title 05. When User Joins Conversation

actor "New Member" as User
participant "New Member\nClient" as Client
participant "Crypto Layer" as Crypto
participant "localStorage" as Storage
participant "Server API" as Server
participant "Database" as DB
participant "Vault KV" as Vault
participant "Helper Client\n(Existing Member)" as Helper

User -> Server: Request to join conversation\n(via invite link or search)
activate Server

Server -> DB: Add member\n{user_id, member_key: NULL, join_date: NOW()}
activate DB
DB --> Server: Member added
deactivate DB

Server --> User: "Added to conversation"
deactivate Server

User -> Client: Fetch conversation
activate Client

Client -> Server: GET /conversations/{conv_id}
activate Server
Server -> DB: Get conversation
activate DB
DB --> Server: {member_key: NULL, ...}
deactivate DB
Server --> Client: Conversation data
deactivate Server

Client -> Client: Detect member_key == NULL

' Now follow same process as requesting group key
Client -> Client: REQUEST GROUP KEY PROCESS\n[Same as Flow 04]
note right of Client
  Identical to "Request Group Key"
  flow using asymmetric encryption
  See diagram 04 for details
end note

' ... asymmetric key exchange happens here ...
Client <-> Helper: Asymmetric group key exchange
Client -> Client: Now has group_key (plaintext)

' Generate new token version
Client -> Crypto: Generate new token
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  token = random(32 bytes)
  New epoch for conversation
  after member join
end note
Crypto --> Client: token (plaintext)
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Crypto: Encrypt token with group_key
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  encrypted_token = Encrypt(
    token,
    group_key
  )
  AES-256-GCM
end note
Crypto --> Client: encrypted_token
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Crypto: Generate member_key
activate Crypto
note right of Crypto
  member_key = Encrypt(
    group_key,
    identity_secret
  )
end note
Crypto --> Client: member_key
deactivate Crypto

Client -> Client: Derive new version name\nfrom previous version\n("v_1.3.4" -> "v_1.3.5")

Client -> Server: POST /conversations/{conv_id}/join-complete\n{member_key, new_token_version, encrypted_token}
activate Server

Server -> Server: Integrity checks:\n- member_key was NULL?\n- User is member?\n- Token version unique?

Server -> Vault: PUT /conversations/{conv_id}/versions/{version}\n{encrypted_token, create_date, created_by}
activate Vault
note right of Vault
  Vault stores encrypted_token
  Cannot decrypt (encrypted with group_key)
end note
Vault --> Server: Stored
deactivate Vault

Server -> DB: UPDATE conversation\nSET member_key = {member_key}\nSET latest_token_version = {version}
activate DB
DB --> Server: Updated
deactivate DB

Server --> Client: "Join complete"
deactivate Server

Client -> Storage: Store encrypted_token
activate Storage
Storage --> Client: Stored
deactivate Storage

Client --> User: "You can now read and send messages"
deactivate Client

note over User, Vault
  Result:
  ✅ New member has group_key
  ✅ New token version created (new epoch)
  ✅ member_key stored (encrypted group_key)
  ✅ Can now read/send messages
  ⚠️ Cannot read messages before join_date
      (authorization prevents access)
end note

@enduml
